Are you an experienced forklift operator who feels right at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to work for a stable company where you’ll work alongside a small, close-knit team to ensure everything runs smoothly? Then we have a great opportunity for you!

For a client in Weert, we’re looking for an experienced forklift operator who enjoys working the night shift. You’ll be joining a large logistics company where safety, teamwork, and a pleasant work environment are top priorities.

What will you be doing?

As a forklift operator, you’ll be responsible for moving goods efficiently and safely within the warehouse. You’ll spend most of your workday operating the forklift. Together with four colleagues, you’ll ensure that all pallets and goods are placed in the correct locations and that outbound orders are ready on time.

Your duties will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking orders and preparing them for shipment;
- Scanning goods;
- Moving pallets and goods within the warehouse;
- Preparing outgoing orders for transport.

You’ll be operating a forklift with double forks, loading from the side. Do you have experience with this? If so, be sure to read on!

You’ve already gained considerable experience operating a forklift and understand how important it is to work safely and accurately. You’re flexible, keep a cool head during busy periods, and are comfortable working two different shifts.

In addition:

- You have recent experience as a forklift operator;
- You hold a valid forklift operator’s certificate;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You are available full-time;
- You work with precision and always put safety first.

SamenvattingReady for the next step in production? Contribute to quality and efficiency! In this role, you are responsible for disassembling, cleaning, testing, and reassembling returned products. This way, you give electronics a second life and directly contribute to a more sustainable process. Do you enjoy varied work and work with precision? Then this is your opportunity!Over de functieYour responsibilities include:
- disassembling returned modems, routers, and parts;
- cleaning components and devices;
- testing individual components and complete products;
- assembling refurbished devices;
- accurately recording test outcomes.

In this company you work from monday to friday, from 07:30 till 16:30.
Over het bedrijfThis company offers comprehensive logistics services with a strong focus on sustainability. They turn returned electronics into valuable refurbished products using high quality and efficient processes.
Wat wij vragen- Energetic and able to stand for 8 hours;
- Interest in electronics and technical tasks;
- Reasonable English language skills;
- Precise, motivated, and team-oriented.

Wat wij bieden- Hourly wage starting from €15.26
- Holiday allowance and vacation hours accrual
- Travel allowance / reimbursement
- High chance of a permanent contract after 6 months
- Realistic opportunities for personal and professional development
- Monthly drinks / social gatherings
- Working in a close-knit and friendly team

